PRE-REGISTRATION -- does the determinism fix GENERALIZE?        2026-09-12
Written BEFORE any 03-lru determinism run.

WHY THIS RUN EXISTS
  Every determinism number in ADR-0157 comes from ONE task, 02-median-bug, chosen
  because it is the CHEAPEST (6 iterations, ~27s). A reproducibility claim measured
  only on the shortest task in the suite is the weakest possible version of itself:
  divergence opportunity grows with token count, so the easy task is exactly where
  byte-identity is most likely for reasons that have nothing to do with the fix.

THE TASK, and why this one
  03-lru. determinism-partition.log names it as THE actionable target: with the
  sampler pinned it still swung 36% in iteration count (15/11/16), the worst
  residual of any deep task, against 04-todo-cli's 0%. It is also 11-16 iterations
  and 261-614s, i.e. 2-3x the length of 02-median-bug.
  NOTE the partition log's pinned arm did NOT have stable_prompt_identity, so its
  36% residual INCLUDES the session-id effect this fix removes. That is precisely
  what makes 03-lru the informative task rather than merely the hard one.

ARMS (real-user configuration in both -- stable workspace, fresh uuid4)
  A  ZAKCODE_TEMPERATURE=0 alone                      (the pre-fix real-user cell)
  B  ZAKCODE_TEMPERATURE=0 + ZAKCODE_STABLE_PROMPT_IDENTITY=1   (with the fix)
  N=3 each. Same instrument as ADR-0157 (bench/determinism_arm.py), which refuses
  a verdict if any run captures zero files.

PREDICTIONS, fixed before data
  G1 Arm A will NOT be byte-identical. It is the pre-fix configuration on a longer
     task; if it IS identical, 03-lru has less divergence opportunity than
     02-median-bug despite being 2-3x longer, and the task choice was wrong.
  G2 Arm B will NOT be byte-identical either. I predict the fix does NOT fully
     generalize: 03-lru carries residual the prompt fix cannot touch, and more
     tokens means more chances for a near-tie to break differently. I expect
     FEWER distinct states than arm A, not one.
  G3 Pass rate is not the measurement. Record it separately; a correctness failure
     is not a determinism result.

DECISION RULES
  B identical AND A not -> the fix generalizes to the hardest known task. ADR-0157's
     claim strengthens from "on 02-median-bug" to "on the task with the worst
     measured residual", and G2 is falsified in the direction that favours the fix --
     which is exactly the direction I must be most suspicious of, so the arms must be
     re-run once before the stronger claim is written.
  B fewer distinct states than A, neither identical -> the fix REDUCES divergence
     without eliminating it. Report both counts. The honest headline then becomes
     task-dependent: byte-reproducible on short tasks, variance-reduced on long ones,
     and ADR-0157's summary line must be amended to say so.
  B == A -> the fix does not help here. The session id was not the barrier on this
     task, ADR-0157's claim is SCOPED TO 02-median-bug, and the generalization is
     withdrawn rather than restated with a caveat.
  EITHER arm failing to capture files -> instrument failure, no verdict (the tool
     already refuses; do not hand-read the digests around it).

WHAT THIS CANNOT DO
  N=3 per arm on one additional task. It can show the fix does or does not survive a
  harder case. It cannot establish a rate, and no rate will be claimed. Two tasks is
  not "generalizes"; it is "did not break on the second one".

ARM C -- added 11:41, BEFORE any 03-lru Claude Code run; arms A/B still unrun
  (paused for pod co-tenancy). Claude Code as it ships, 03-lru, N=3. Runs off-pod
  (Anthropic API), so it does not contend with the TOPK eval.
  G4 Arm C will NOT be byte-identical: at least 2 distinct output states of 3,
     matching its 02-median-bug behaviour (2 states in each of 2 batches).
  G5 Arm C passes 3/3 -- correctness is not the variable, same as every cell so far.
  Decision: G4 holds -> the reference arm's nondeterminism is not task-specific
     either, and the A/B/C comparison on 03-lru is a like-for-like three-way.
     G4 fails (identical 3/3) -> Claude Code is byte-stable on the HARDER task,
     which would be the more surprising result and must be reported over the
     02-median-bug one, not beside it.

